    <article class="article-card reveal" id="offline-first-education-tools" data-writing="offline first education tools learning classrooms sync connectivity">
      <div class="article-meta">
        <span class="date">October 2025</span>
        <span class="tag brand">Education</span>
        <span class="tag warm">Offline-First</span>
        <span class="read-time">5 min read</span>
      </div>
      <h2>Offline-First Is a Pedagogical Decision, Not Just a Technical One</h2>
      <p class="lead lead-spaced">
        Connectivity constraints change classroom behavior. If software degrades under poor internet conditions,
        learning time is lost and trust in the tool drops quickly.
      </p>
      <h3>What Good Offline Design Looks Like</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Core learning paths stay available with zero network dependency.</li>
        <li>Local storage keeps progress safe until sync is possible.</li>
        <li>Teachers can still monitor essential progress signals offline.</li>
        <li>Sync conflicts are visible and recoverable, not hidden.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="related-links">
        <p>Related reading</p>
        <ul>
